    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Unlocking _everything_ on the CPU with DRAM scrambling",
      "url": "https://github.com/xoreaxeaxeax/skitter-creek-bath-salts",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/a4zifd",
      "score": 54,
      "comments": 17,
      "author": "radex",
      "published": "2026-08-13T16:06:04Z",
      "bullets": [
        "DRAM scrambling algorithms, designed for EMI reduction, can be reversed to manipulate memory contents and bypass architectural access controls.",
        "Weak PRNG-based scrambling enables physical memory fault injection, exposing secure enclaves and platform firmware keys to physical attackers.",
        "Defenses require authenticated, cryptographic memory encryption like Intel TME or AMD SME rather than reliance on pseudo-random DRAM scrambling."
      ]
    },
